    "recommendations": "• Install a reflective address marker at the road entrance to the driveway so responders can identify the property quickly from the road.\n• Mark the driveway entrance with reflective posts on both sides to define its edges at night or in low-visibility conditions.\n• Keep the circular driveway clear of parked vehicles so arriving apparatus can pull forward and turn without obstruction.\n• Post the property address visibly at the driveway entrance, not only at the house, given the length of the drive.\n• Identify and mark any secondary foot access point to the rear of the property so responders are not limited to the single vehicle access drive.\n• Keep the lawn and open areas free of equipment, materials, or vehicles that would reduce available staging space for apparatus and crews."
