    "recommendations": "• Trim shrubs that are growing close to the house on any side where branches or stems touch or nearly touch the exterior.\n• Thin scattered trees near the structure so their canopies do not overlap or connect with each other.\n• Cut grass around the house and outbuildings regularly, especially during dry months when it dries out and lies flat.\n• Remove or thin brush in the area behind the house where rear access is limited, to make that space easier to move through.\n• Keep the long driveway clear of overhanging branches from edge trees and shrubs so vehicles can pass without obstruction.\n• Trim back any shrubs or low branches that narrow the driveway or reduce visibility along its length.\n• Mark the driveway entrance clearly so it is easy to locate when approaching from the main road.\n• Move any wood piles, stored materials, or flammable objects away from the house and outbuildings.\n• Keep irrigated landscaping beds directly next to the house free of dead leaves, dry mulch, and dry plant stems.\n• Separate shrubs in the brush area from any nearby structures by removing plants closest to those structures first.\n• Clear a walking path around the back of the house so the rear can be reached on foot without pushing through dense vegetation."
